33,34$ 33a : On herbaceous stems.
33,35$ 33b : On wood, leaves, needles or fruits.
34,0$ 34a : Apothecia opening by an elongate slit. On Filipendula. $ Holmiodiscus. $s"Holmiodiscus."
34,0$ 34b : Apothecia opening by a pore. On herbaceous stems, preferably of Apiaceae. $ Heterosphaeria. $s"Heterosphaeria."
35,36$ 35a : Sp aseptate.
35,38$ 35b : Sp 1-7-septate.
36,0$ 36a : On dead needles, twigs or branches of conifers. Apothecia 1-3 mm broad. $ Cenangium. $s"Cenangium."
36,37$ 36b : On deciduous wood. Apothecia often larger.
37,0$ 37a : Pigment soluble and turning reddish brown in KOH. $ Ionomidotis. $s"Ionomidotis."
37,0$ 37b : Pigment not soluble and turning reddish brown in KOH. $ See Encoelia.
38,0$ 38a : On dead leaves and twigs of Ledum. $ Neogodronia. $s"Neogodronia."
38,39$ 38b : On other substrates.
39,0$ 39a : Sp 15-20 x 3-4 µm. On dead twigs of Calluna. $ Erikssonopsis. $s"Erikssonopsis."
39,40$ 39b : Sp > 20 µm long. On various substrates.
40,0$ 40a : Sp 6-8 µm broad. Frb developing from widely effused, black stroma on Betula. $ Dencoeliopsis. $s"Dencoeliopsis."
40,0$ 40b : Sp 1-5 µm broad. Stroma present or absent ; on various hosts. $ Godronia p.p. $s"Godronia p.p."
41,42$ 41a : Frb sessile, saucer-shaped, blackish or red.
41,43$ 41b : Frb sessile or stipitate, not saucer-shaped, with paler colours.
42,0$ 42a : Apothecia seated on a red subiculum. $ Patinellaria. $s"Patinellaria."
